      "result": "\n\nDone. The complete C source has been written to `submission/main.c`.\n\nSummary of how it meets each requirement:\n\n1. **I2C bus from devicetree** — `DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_NODELABEL(i2c0))`\n2. **Ready check** — `device_is_ready(i2c_dev)`, returning `-ENODEV` if not ready\n3. **Sensor address** — `#define SENSOR_I2C_ADDRESS 0x68` (7-bit)\n4. **Register address** — `#define WHO_AM_I_REG 0x75`\n5. **Byte read** — `i2c_reg_read_byte(i2c_dev, SENSOR_I2C_ADDRESS, WHO_AM_I_REG, &who_am_i)`\n6. **Error check** — `err != 0` is tested after the call\n7. **Success print** — `printk(\"WHO_AM_I register value: 0x%02x\\n\", who_am_i)`\n8. **Failure print** — `printk(\"Failed to read WHO_AM_I register: %d\\n\", err)`\n9. **Return codes** — `return 0` on success, `return err` (negative error code) on failure\n\nHeaders included: `<zephyr/kernel.h>`, `<zephyr/device.h>`, `<zephyr/drivers/i2c.h>`.",
